        <p>So Iz in i t„ ch nternational interest just now is cen- lit7 11l the American yacht Navahoe, that it seems "He to hear that Mr. Carroll's fellow-memberi of the New York Yacht Club are secretly hoping bh" the craft will either not compete with Lord •raekinraven's Valkyrie for the Cape May Cup, or be if th Y beaten,and on this score. It is argued that e Navahoe wins, her victory will greatly serve eohet'"en the interest in the great coming event, the „ eBt for the American Cup, since there are on to‘te Other side" several yachts which are known faster sailers than the Navahoe, in which case Dunraven will be easily defeated.</p>
