        <p>THE G. F. McCORQUODALE CHALLENGE CUP. NEWTON PRINTING WORKS v. CARDINOTON-ST. Wonxs. —The final con:petition for the challenge cup offered by Messrs. McCorquodale and Co., was played on Monday at Wormwood Scrubs, London, between teams repre- senting the Newton and London departments of the firm. The Leeds Works have previously proved the victors and are now the holders of one cup. The one played for on Saturday is a new cup, and Newton have been fortunate in becoming, the holders for this rear. The teams were selected 'solely from employes in the works, and the Newton team journeyed to London on Saturday. The London men batted first, and on the Newton men going in, things looked rather black. 4 wickets being down for 16 runs. Ball and Wilkinson however made a good stand, and changed the aspect of affairs, 50 runs being scored for the fall of the fifth wicket, and Newton eventu- ally won by 26 suns. Harrison for Newton handled the leather successfully. taking 7 wickets for 25 runs, while Yuill, for Cardington-st., secured 7 tor 29. Scores : CA.RDINGTON-ST. NEWTON. Wells a Hindley b Earn- Parks b Yuill BOR l7 J Ball b Yuill , Grumbridgeb Harrison... 0 Harrison b Burr Cookson 0 and b Hindley 1- Hlndiey lbw bYuill 7 Hill c Hindley b Mills ... 35 H Ball bYuill Wilson lbw b Harrison ... 0 Wilkinson c Bettles b Yuill 21 Crewe run out Settles b Harrison ' 3 Mills b Yulll 3 o Lindsay b Harrison lB Pearson bYuill ' o Yuill not out 4. Owen b Hill 2 Reeve a Hindley b Hare- Kidd not out 0 son Durr a Parks to Harrison 0 Extras ......</p>
