        <p>At the conclusion of the match the players adjourned to the Viaduct Hotel, where they sat down:and heartily enjoyed an excellent dinner provided by Mr. A Tunstall, in his best style. After dinner a somat evening was spent, the President of the Institute Club, Mr. Joseph Emmett, presiding over the proceedings, whilst the vice chair was occupied by Mr. W. Cooper, captain of the visiting team. The Chairman in proposing the health of the visitors, said although they, had suffered defeat,he hoped they would do better next time they met.</p>
