        <p>As WROLESALE MURDERS FOR GAIN. saes, h„.1,4r On Papers report the arrest in aYi Detroit of Dr. ,—„e3:_er, and his supposed wife Mary,which brings o thse-,Ztaing story of the poisoning of men and women lb.l the ir,:lirP°se of collecting insurance upon their lives. Oh a 'lt of the facts collected by the detectives the qa34ol3Pears as a cruel and calculating scoundrel, who 1 tbt„besitated to kill a number of Dcrsons for money, 94ta. ft woman is portrayed as a second Lucretia Boy- "!nlan's career of crime is said to have begun in 04(14e"1:11 graduated a year before at the Chicago Ham ceo- -1878, when he poisoned his first wife. He IZ4,tti 07,"01, but had not been able to obtain much A physician. After getting rid of his wife he Man named Gederman, in order to marry Widow. Then he poisoned the woman's :tta V 1,4 later the woman herself. Another woman i s n w to hi toils as taken to Toledo, and poisoned 41.tsi`beln_s_u.ranc e on her life. The woman who has Slid RN's 'mown as his wife formerly lived in Indian- accompanied him to Chicago a few years ago. • "le his Nvilline, tool in the poisoning of men for ci• t• Associated w'ith them in Chicago was Ludwig a'7ltip ' a German, who had made a precarious living by LNtidg st`lties for German papers and magazines. A tO Brandt named Winimer also became interested •ili4sl,,..elsurance frauds. Under a insured names Brandt ...'llipa,:f4Mer would have their lives in several d7all ci'ws• Then i they would fall sick, taking poison n °ses at the instigation of Dr. Meyer, in order to k`°,lsr.,',,P_llYs.i•zians who were called to attend them. At ll gcl Per L time the corpses of other men were obtained itlt,—S,pBtl 017 as the bodies of the men who had been he bodies would be buried with a show of grief iktatld‘st'a-01cieser,. mmer• who nosed in turn as the widow of of Wi Sbe would also collect the Inoney. In order to get ff 'Or)• `4Ce bodies to pass oas h atidt and Wimmer the poisoners killed Gee- appearances tallied closely with that of the It was for the supposed poisoning of 0111,.iL114(1.er the name of Gustav H. J. Baum, in New 00(1" Meyer, and his wife were arrested in Detroit. flame of Bu m, Brandt had his life insured by °l4al-411Panlen aaust 13, 1891. The polices were tea ..„ees in AI.I Chicago for the following amounts: o't Vetliat ?fk Life, I,ooodols, £tna Life, I,ooodols.</p>
        <p>•ttemtLife 't xritna 141 d 3,500d015. ; and Washington Life, 3,000d01s th, ~'elared that he was soon to be married, and EZ' made out in favour of his wire. The Njhu„tl.found an indictment for murder in the first Nl:•!nst Henry Meyer, alias William Rattier, alias ers, alias Henry Maylor, and Maria Meyer, laUrn, alias Marie Meyets, far giving thirty tA4e92. antimony to Gustav H. Joseph Baum on March' tcit, 1,411)r. Meyer's wifo was taken to an hospital in ere she gave birth to a child.</p>
