        <p>MARRIAGES. Pc:j4t- ""lect c • 4rnmlttee of the House of Commons ap- kta „ nsider the question of the presence of re- Conformist marriages have presented their zii.oit4i It states that the Committee have come to till t`3l4, tryr(4l. that the compulsory attendance of the civil 4t. Nonconformist marriages is felt by Noncon- OE pp generally to be a serious grievance, and ono large numbers of Nonconformists being ti.lngst ,Lueir own own places of worship. They state things that the attendance of the rogis- t,llfcr,;.condition of the validity of marriages in Non- aces of worship is neither desirable norne- the purpose of securing accurate registration i4tl tl,he best plan for securing such accurate registra- -41,°3t be to make it the duty of the person officiat- cl th4,rnarriage to register it himself. They recom- ')i an- alteration of the law should be made in th,7titki..lll) as to reserve to Nonconformists the option -Ing that the registrar should attend as required</p>
