        <p>for his gift of the Mayor's chair and pendant passed by the Town Council on the sixth ult. be engrossed and presented to him .—Alderman Wareing in proposing the minutes said the interview with Mr. Shaw was extremely ' satisfactory, and they gathered that he would do his best to meet their wishes. As to Mr. Pollitt that gentle- man appeared to be under misapprehension. As to engrossing the vote of thanks ta the Mayor this would emphasise the appreciation the Council entertained of His Warship's generous gift.—Councillor Shores seconded.—Carried. FINANCE. The Finance Committee reported that the balance due to the bank was £1,099 Ss. 3d. The collections for the month amounted to £10,112 10s. sd. Accounts amount- ing to £3,958 165., were examined and passed for pay- ment. The minutes were approved on the motion of Coun- cillor Owens. LATEST NE WS. MR. It USKIN'S HEALTH.</p>
